      "name": "Quick Bolognese with Fresh Spring Pasta",
      "source_url": "https://www.seriouseats.com/the-best-slow-cooked-bolognese-sauce-recipe",
      "source_name": "Serious Eats (quick-adapted)",
      "servings": "4 to 6",
      "prep_time": "20 minutes",
      "cook_time": "1 hour",
      "nonna_says": "Start the soffritto first and let it soften till sweet, because a rushed onion tastes like punishment. Add the pancetta, then brown the beef and pork hard enough to get color, not gray sadness. Stir in the tomato paste, wine, tomatoes, stock, and milk, then let it bubble down till thick and brick red. Boil the fresh pasta only a minute or two, then finish it in the sauce with pasta water so everything marries properly. Do not dump naked pasta on a plate and spoon sauce on top like a cafeteria line. Shower it with pecorino and serve while the pot is still talking.",
      "variations": [
